  "details": "It is extremely unintuitive to hold down tab and while holding it, drag your cursor over to the hamburger menu. I suspect that a lot of people will find this cumbersome versus pressing the escape key on your keyboard to summon a menu.\n\nThe alternative to this would be at the very least to show the microphone and invite/notification icons with the new desktop HUD disabled. Disabling the HUD is the only way to get rid of the hamburger menu. One can argue that a microphone icon is a HUD element. But, so is face mirror and that is de-coupled from the new HUD layout.",
